{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T01:49:12.779Z","ordinal":274,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18032-74cb-7ba3-a53c-bbaba01fd9c0","call_id":"call_e27cd22b77ce4bf28eba60b06bffb7b0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation. (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33325828/)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation. ... Publication date: 2020 Dec 16 ...   * Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: last week; Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6} ... Translation, Cross-Cultural Adaptation, and Validation of the Malay Version of the System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the Assessment of Mobile Apps. ... URL: https://www.usability.gov/how-to-and-tools/methods/system-usability-scale.html [accessed 2020-09-11] 13], there is no evidence of the validity and reliability process. ... Second, to achieve the forward translation, the original version of the SUS was translated into Spanish by 2 independent translators with an adequate understanding of the source language: one individual had a master’s degree in translation studies and the other was a professional certified in English language and linguistics whose native language was Spanish. ... In this study, a Spanish version of the SUS questionnaire was developed and validated. ... URL: https://www.who.int/goe/publications/goe_mhealth_web.pdf [accessed 2020-12-08]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Preprints #21161: System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools: Development and validation of a Spanish version (https://preprints.jmir.org/preprint/21161/accepted)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.0 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Sevilla-Gonzalez M, Moreno-Loaeza L, Lazaro-Carrera LS, Bourguet-Ramírez B, Vázquez-Rodríguez A, Peralta-Pedrero ML, Almeda-Valdés P\n\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... ## System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools: Development and validation of a Spanish version ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... The content validity index of the new Spanish SUS was good based on the rating of the relevance of items of 0.92.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation - PMC (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7773510/)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n### Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez, MSc, PhD ... This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work, first published in JMIR Human Factors, is properly cited. ... The System Usability Scale (SUS) proposed by Brooke [9] in 1986 is a widely used questionnaire to assess the usability of a system, such as standard operating system–based software interfaces, webpages, and mobile apps. ... In this study, a Spanish version of the SUS questionnaire was developed and validated.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsability as a Premise of Quality: First Steps Towards the Validation of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish | Journal of Audiovisual Translation (https://jatjournal.org/index.php/jat/article/view/77)\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.8 years ago; Crawled: last month;   * Irene Tor-Carroggio Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2924-014X ... usability, usability evaluation, SUS, system usability scale, Spanish, questionnaire translation, questionnaire validation ... Originally designed in English, it is available in some other languages, such as Persian and Greek but no validated version in Spanish can be found yet.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/authors)\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/citations)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: today; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/org/science/article/pii/S2292949520000395)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... The System Usability Scale (SUS) is a common metric used to assess the usability of a system, and it was initially developed in English. ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... The CVI (Table 1) and FVI (Table 2) of the new Spanish version of the SUS were calculated to be 0.92 and 0.94, respectively.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSG3._Bruno_Rios_-_Prueba_de_concepto (https://revistas.ulima.edu.pe/index.php/Interfases/article/download/6557/6883/30221?inline=1)\nciteturn0search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Preguntas del cuestionario SUS validadas al español ... Tomado de Sevilla-González et al. (2020).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Preprints #21161: Translation, cross-cultural adaptation and validation of the System Usability Scale questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools “SUS”, to a new Spanish version (https://preprints.jmir.org/preprint/21161/submitted)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Sevilla-Gonzalez M, Moreno-Loaeza L, Lazaro-Carrera LS, Bourguet-Ramírez B, Vázquez-Rodríguez A, Peralta-Pedrero ML, Almeda-Valdés P ... ## Translation, cross-cultural adaptation and validation of the System Usability Scale questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools “SUS”, to a new Spanish version ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... According to Cronbach’s alpha test 0.81 IC95% (0.74 – 0.86), the translated scale is s a reliable tool for the assessment of the usability of electronic tools.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/tweetations)\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: last month; Image: Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n# Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/metrics)\nciteturn0search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTYPE Original Research (https://zaguan.unizar.es/record/170231/files/texto_completo.pdf)\nciteturn0search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; In the absence of a formally published Spanish validation ... Memory Questionnaire (PRMQ-S), originally developed by (Smith \net al., 2000) and subsequently adapted and validated for Spanish- ... Spanish version of the System Usability Scale (SUS), created by (Brooke, ... populations by (Sevilla-Gonzalez et al., 2020).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDiseño, desarrollo y (https://riubu.ubu.es/bitstream/10259/9555/1/Yanez_Perez_Iraya-Tesis.pdf)\nciteturn0search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; For the quantitative strand of the research, the System Usability Scale (SUS, ... The Spanish \nversion of the questionnaire was used (Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez et al., 2020). ... multiplied by 2.5 to obtain a scale ranging from 0 to 100.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsability as a Premise of Quality: (https://ddd.uab.cat/pub/artpub/2019/216459/document.pdf)\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; First Steps Towards the Validation of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish ... Lastly, some commentaries about the questionnaire design ... Spanish version of SUS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSevilla-Gonzalez et al (https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/efa7/7e1cf21b4bab9653c2194b7b4007528fbfb1.pdf)\nciteturn0search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez1,2,3, MSc, PhD; Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza3, MSc; Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera3, ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... (JMIR Hum Factors 2020;7(4):e21161) doi: 10.2196/21161 ... mHealth; usability; validation; System Usability Scale; Spanish\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPRE-PRINT COPY (https://roderic.uv.es/rest/api/core/bitstreams/2c779123-6ff8-494e-a060-2dcc410134ed/content)\nciteturn0search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; were considered (CFI=.932, TLI=.898; RMSEA=.055, CI 90%= 0.047, 0.062), ... items in the structure of the SUS and propose a short version of the SUS to be ... Keywords: System Usability Scale, validity, reliability, method effects, Spanish,\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAntwerp, 25/08/2021 (https://u-pad.unimc.it/retrieve/handle/11393/299007/2a98993e-5120-4bb6-8a0d-c3104861a994/10%20Greco_Jankowska_JAT_special_issue_2019.pdf)\nciteturn0search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.2 years ago; of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish ... the validation of the System Usability ... but no validated version in Spanish can be found yet. ... questionnaire ...  Irene.Tor@uab.cat, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2924-014X\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrueba de usabilidad (https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prueba_de_usabilidad)\nciteturn0search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.9 years ago; * SUS (System Usability Scale): es una herramienta rápida y fiable para medir la usabilidad. ... En 2023 se ha validado el cuestionario en español (10 ítems), así como una versión corta de 5 ítems ... «Psychometric Properties of the Spanish Full and Short Forms of the System Usability Scale (SUS): Detecting the Effect of Negatively Worded Items». ... ISBN 0-8058-3290-4.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSystem usability scale (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_usability_scale)\nciteturn0search19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago;  Standard version of the system usability scale ... The final SUS score can be computed with the following formula:${\\displaystyle SUS=2.5\\left(20+\\sum ({\\text{SUS01}},{\\text{SUS03}},{\\text{SUS05}},{\\text{SUS07}},{\\text{SUS09}})-\\sum ({\\text{SUS02}},{\\text{SUS04}},{\\text{SUS06}},{\\text{SUS08}},{\\text{SUS10}})\\right)}$ ... Because it yields a single score on a scale of 0–100, it can be used to compare even systems that are outwardly dissimilar. This one-dimensional aspect of the SUS is both a benefit and a drawback because the questionnaire is necessarily quite general. ... The factor structure of the system usability scale (PDF).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQuestionnaire for User Interaction Satisfaction (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Questionnaire_for_User_Interaction_Satisfaction)\nciteturn0search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 11 months ago; The QUIS is currently at Version 7.0 with demographic questionnaire, a measure of overall system satisfaction along 6 scales, and measures of 9 specific interface factors. ... In addition to English, the QUIS 7.0 is currently available in the following languages: German, Italian, Portuguese (Brazilian), and Spanish. ... * System Usability Scale (SUS) ... The QUIS Version 7.0 is an updated and expanded version of the previously validated QUIS 5.5.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152152.7792287}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
